# Pre-commit CSharpier format

When the user asks you to **create a commit**, format C# changes first if this repository contains C# code.

**Team formatter:** [CSharpier](https://csharpier.com) — **Cursor extension** for day-to-day edits; **repo-local CLI** (`.config/dotnet-tools.json`, pinned version) for agents and scripts. Style from `.editorconfig`.

## Does this repo have C#?

Same gate as `post-commit-csharp-code-review.mdc`:

- `**/*.cs` (exclude `Library/`, `obj/`, `bin/`)
- or `*.csproj` / `*.sln`

If **none** apply, skip and commit per user git instructions.

## Required workflow (C# repos)

1. Gather commit scope: `git status`, `git diff` — list every `.cs` path in the commit (staged + unstaged).
2. If the commit includes **no** `.cs` changes, skip formatting.
3. **Format before commit** (order: CSharpier → `git commit` → post-commit code review per `post-commit-csharp-code-review.mdc`):
   - Follow the **csharpier-format** agent skill.
   - From the **repository root** (Unity: folder with `Assets/` and `.config/dotnet-tools.json`), on **changed paths only**:
     ```powershell
     dotnet tool restore
     dotnet csharpier format path/to/File.cs
     ```
   - Use the **local tool** first; fall back to global `csharpier format` only if the manifest is missing.
   - CLI output should match **Format Document** with the CSharpier extension on the same files.
4. Re-run `git diff` after formatting; include formatting-only changes in the commit unless the user excludes them.
5. After commit, continue with `post-commit-csharp-code-review.mdc` if `.cs` was in the commit.

## If CLI is unavailable

Do not substitute another formatter. Tell the user to format the listed `.cs` files in Cursor (**Format Document** with CSharpier as default formatter), then re-check `git diff` before committing.

## Exceptions

- User explicitly requests **commit without formatting** or **skip format**.
- Commit scope is **only** non-C# files in an otherwise C# repo.

## Out of scope

- `.uxml`, shaders, YAML — C# only.
- PR-only workflows unless the user asks to format there too.
